---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { TOOLS } from '../data/tools';
---
<PageLayout
  title="About HugMyFile – Free Tools That Respect You"
  description="Why HugMyFile exists: free, unlimited file tools with no signup and no watermark that run in your browser, so your files never leave your device."
  path="/about"
  h1="About HugMyFile"
  lead="We hug your files. We never keep them."
>
  <p>
    HugMyFile is a collection of {TOOLS.length} everyday file tools for images, PDFs, QR codes, signatures and text recognition.
    It started from a simple frustration: the features people need most, like compressing a batch of photos, signing a PDF or
    adding a logo to a QR code, are often hidden behind accounts, daily limits, watermarks or paid plans.
  </p>
  <p>We think those basics should be free, unlimited and private. So we built them that way.</p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Every tool on this site runs inside your web browser. When you choose a file, your own device does the work using
    well-known open-source libraries compiled to run in the browser. There is no upload step and no server that receives your
    files, which means there is nothing for us to store, leak or delete.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because the work happens on your device, speed depends on your computer or phone. Most tasks finish in a moment; very large
    files or text recognition may take a little longer on older phones.
  </p>

  <h2>Our promises</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Runs on your device.</strong> Your files are processed locally and never leave your browser.</li>
    <li><strong>Free.</strong> All tools are free to use, as often as you like, with no daily caps.</li>
    <li><strong>No signup.</strong> There are no accounts and no logins anywhere on the site.</li>
    <li><strong>No watermark.</strong> We never put our name or logo on your results.</li>
    <li><strong>Honest about limits.</strong> If a tool cannot do something well (like a compression that would not help), it tells you plainly.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we keep the lights on</h2>
  <p>
    Running a fast website still costs a little. In the future the site may show a small number of clearly labeled ads from
    Google AdSense. Ads will never be placed on top of a tool or disguised as buttons, and they never get access to your files.
    You can read exactly what that means in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Built on open source</h2>
  <p>
    HugMyFile stands on the shoulders of excellent open-source projects. You can see every library, font and data file we use,
    along with its license, on our <a href="/licenses">Open-source credits</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>Say hello</h2>
  <p>Found a bug or have an idea for a tool? We would love to hear from you on our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
